{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017njSQNxGQpqcQwJsgKMoRT","type":"tool_result","content":"290\t  that already have them, restore skips such a member, without writing\n291\t  it, only when its matching file or folder is in the same archive; any\n292\t  other `._` member is refused. Restore now extracts only the members it\n293\t  accepted, in Python instead of with `tar -x`: a truncated or corrupt\n294\t  archive is refused before anything is written, and so is an archive\n295\t  with a sparse member or with two members of the same name.\n296\t- The disaster-recovery and incident-response guides no longer pass\n297\t  `--dry-run`, a flag the script refuses. The preview is the default, and\n298\t  `--apply` restores.\n299\t\n300\t### Fixed — `audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter`\n301\t\n302\t- With the flag, every result maps to a documented exit code with a named\n303\t  reason, one JSON object under `--json`, and no traceback.\n304\t- An absent counter exits 0 and reports `chain_length_source: \"absent\"`.\n305\t  An unreadable counter exits 3.\n306\t- A file and stdin go through one strict decode, and a log that is not a\n307\t  regular file is refused.\n308\t- Without the flag, nothing changes.\n309\t\n310\t### Fixed — three findings of the v1.4.3-rc.1 re-pass\n311\t\n312\t- `diagnose-output-hook.py` can no longer write to the live audit log.\n313\t- `check-audit-real-loss.py` reports a malformed `record_id` instead of\n314\t  crashing.\n315\t- `audit_spool_state.py` and `check-audit-real-loss.py`, both read-only,\n316\t  stop writing bytecode.\n317\t\n318\t### Fixed — harness gate, root `CLAUDE.md` exclusion, plan lifecycle, cost envelope\n319\t\n320\t- `check-active-hooks-executable.py` validates a hook's `type` and\n321\t  `matcher` the way the loader does. A settings path that exists but is\n322\t  not a regular file, and a filesystem error while resolving a hook path,\n323\t  exit 2 with a named error.\n324\t- `check_harness_config.py` turns an exception in that sub-check into a\n325\t  RED finding and keeps its output. Before, it was a degraded warning,\n326\t  which reads as green.\n327\t- A `claudeMdExcludes` value that excludes the root `CLAUDE.md` is\n328\t  classified as settings tamper (`settings_tamper_claude_md_excludes_root`).\n329\t- The harness gate adds an advisory finding, `root_instruction_load`. It"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"491a10bf-cca8-4c48-ae81-b32fc5bafb56","uuid":"f977027f-0df3-4339-8f5c-7cf2607ec0de","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:13:20.084Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/CHANGELOG.md","content":"  that already have them, restore skips such a member, without writing\n  it, only when its matching file or folder is in the same archive; any\n  other `._` member is refused. Restore now extracts only the members it\n  accepted, in Python instead of with `tar -x`: a truncated or corrupt\n  archive is refused before anything is written, and so is an archive\n  with a sparse member or with two members of the same name.\n- The disaster-recovery and incident-response guides no longer pass\n  `--dry-run`, a flag the script refuses. The preview is the default, and\n  `--apply` restores.\n\n### Fixed — `audit-verify-chain.py --strict-against-counter`\n\n- With the flag, every result maps to a documented exit code with a named\n  reason, one JSON object under `--json`, and no traceback.\n- An absent counter exits 0 and reports `chain_length_source: \"absent\"`.\n  An unreadable counter exits 3.\n- A file and stdin go through one strict decode, and a log that is not a\n  regular file is refused.\n- Without the flag, nothing changes.\n\n### Fixed — three findings of the v1.4.3-rc.1 re-pass\n\n- `diagnose-output-hook.py` can no longer write to the live audit log.\n- `check-audit-real-loss.py` reports a malformed `record_id` instead of\n  crashing.\n- `audit_spool_state.py` and `check-audit-real-loss.py`, both read-only,\n  stop writing bytecode.\n\n### Fixed — harness gate, root `CLAUDE.md` exclusion, plan lifecycle, cost envelope\n\n- `check-active-hooks-executable.py` validates a hook's `type` and\n  `matcher` the way the loader does. A settings path that exists but is\n  not a regular file, and a filesystem error while resolving a hook path,\n  exit 2 with a named error.\n- `check_harness_config.py` turns an exception in that sub-check into a\n  RED finding and keeps its output. Before, it was a degraded warning,\n  which reads as green.\n- A `claudeMdExcludes` value that excludes the root `CLAUDE.md` is\n  classified as settings tamper (`settings_tamper_claude_md_excludes_root`).\n- The harness gate adds an advisory finding, `root_instruction_load`. It","numLines":40,"startLine":290,"totalLines":2658}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017njSQNxGQpqcQwJsgKMoRT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
