{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FaJ5ELEsuLV5uW8UfsrT4v","type":"tool_result","content":"271:def chain_length_path() -> Path:\n272-    \"\"\"Return the chain-length canary sidecar path.\n273-\n274-    PLAN-045 Wave 1 F-01-05: monotonic counter of HMAC-bearing entries\n275-    written to the log. Allows ``verify_chain`` ``--strict`` mode to\n276-    detect tail truncation even when the remaining log + sidecar are\n277-    internally consistent.\n278-\n279-    ``CEO_AUDIT_CHAIN_LENGTH_PATH`` env override mirrors the other\n280-    audit-log sidecar path helpers for test isolation.\n281-    \"\"\"\n282-    override = os.environ.get(\"CEO_AUDIT_CHAIN_LENGTH_PATH\")\n283-    if override:\n284-        return Path(override)\n285-    return _audit_dir_from_env() / CHAIN_LENGTH_FILENAME\n286-\n287-\n288-def _check_perm_0600(p: Path) -> None:\n289-    \"\"\"Raise AuditHmacError on unsafe permissions, ownership, or symlinks.\n290-\n291-    PLAN-045 Wave 1 F-01-06 hardening:\n292-\n293-    1. **Symlink reject.** A 0600 symlink pointing to an attacker file\n294-       passes a naive mode check; reject any symlink leaf outright.\n295-    2. **Ownership check.** ``st_uid == os.getuid()``. On a multi-user\n296-       host, a 0600 file owned by a different user (e.g. inherited via\n297-       ``chown`` after a hostile ``git stash pop``) previously passed\n298-       this check; now it fails.\n299-    3. **Group/world bits.** Retained from the existing check\n300-       (security-engineer review §2): ``mode & 0o077 != 0`` fails.\n301-\n302-    Parent-dir perms are validated at the caller in\n303-    :func:`get_or_create_key` via ``parent.mkdir(mode=0o700)``; a parent\n304-    created with different perms will be re-mkdir'd (mkdir is idempotent\n305-    only on existence, not perms — the mode arg has no effect once the\n306-    dir exists). The belt-and-suspenders parent-dir check is in\n307-    :func:`_check_parent_dir_owned_0700` for callers that want it.\n308-    \"\"\"\n309-    try:\n310-        if p.is_symlink():\n311-            raise AuditHmacError(\n--\n596:def read_chain_length() -> int:\n597-    \"\"\"Return the persisted chain-length counter, or 0 if absent/malformed.\n598-\n599-    Fail-open: a missing or corrupt sidecar returns 0 (the genesis\n600-    value). ``verify_chain(strict_against_counter=True)`` treats any\n601-    walker-count >= returned-counter as pass; counter > walker indicates\n602-    tail truncation and fails-closed.\n603-\n604-    MUST be called WITH the audit-log FileLock held.\n605-    \"\"\"\n606-    p = chain_length_path()\n607-    if not p.exists():\n608-        return 0\n609-    try:\n610-        raw = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").strip()\n611-    except OSError:\n612-        return 0\n613-    if not raw:\n614-        return 0\n615-    try:\n616-        n = int(raw)\n617-    except ValueError:\n618-        return 0\n619-    if n < 0:\n620-        return 0\n621-    return n\n622-\n623-\n624-def write_chain_length(n: int) -> None:\n625-    \"\"\"Persist the chain-length counter (atomic rename, 0600 perms).\n626-\n627-    Called by ``audit_emit._write_event`` after each successful HMAC\n628-    entry write. Monotonic; caller is responsible for incrementing\n629-    against ``read_chain_length() + 1``.\n630-\n631-    Fail-open: raises ``AuditHmacError`` so the caller can decide\n632-    whether to skip the canary update (fail-open) or propagate. The\n633-    canary is a detection aid, not a correctness requirement.\n634-\n635-    MUST be called WITH the audit-log FileLock held.\n636-    \"\"\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"491a10bf-cca8-4c48-ae81-b32fc5bafb56","uuid":"08b80f4b-7fac-4503-8cd3-c81bb681fe12","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:13:22.537Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"271:def chain_length_path() -> Path:\n272-    \"\"\"Return the chain-length canary sidecar path.\n273-\n274-    PLAN-045 Wave 1 F-01-05: mon