 second in-process main([... '--stdin', '--strict-against-counter']) call finds stdin closed. Fix: detach() the wrapper instead of close() when it wraps stdin.\\n6. P2 (cosmetic) — .claude/scripts/audit-query.py:391. The comment \\\"# Default window for by-domain ...\\\" is now orphaned, because the constant moved to _lib/_audit_query/domain.py. Same for the section banner above it. Fix: delete or point it to domain.py.\",\"decision\":\"GO\",\"sentence\":\"Condition 3(c) holds against the code and condition 7 matches the facades. The audit-query and budget-summary facades keep names, globals, patch points, __file__-relative paths and the freeze-guard surface. The strict audit-verify-chain mode closes on input it cannot read and leaves the non-flag path unchanged. Only documentation and maintenance P2 items remain, with no P0 or P1 in this payload.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"PAYLOAD 24/32: review of v1.4.3-rc.1..5805af55. Files: .claude/scripts/audit-query.py, audit-verify-chain.py, audit_spool_state.py, budget-summary.py and caller_repo_guard.py (new). I read the extracted modules in the candidate tree as well: .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_query/*, .claude/hooks/_lib/_budget_summary_parts/*, scripts/install.sh, scripts/build-plugin.py, .claude/scripts/mcp-server/handlers/audit_query.py and .claude/scripts/check-audit-read-api-stable.py.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS CHECKED AGAINST THIS PAYLOAD\n- Condition 3(c) is TRUE. audit_spool_state.py:62 sets sys.dont_write_bytecode = True before the sys.path walk and before `from _lib import runtime_paths` (line 69). check-audit-real-loss.py sets it at line 67, before `import audit_spool_state` (line 71). No hook imports audit_spool_state, so flipping this global affects only the two read-only CLIs.\n- Condition 7 is consistent. audit-query.py and budget-summary.py keep their paths and become facades over the new _lib packages. scripts/install.sh:1520-1549 (install_lib_selective) copies every top-level _lib entry, subdirectori